// The Weather Engine (docs/DECKS.md 3.3: Engineer, band III, needs Machinery; 10.2a and 10.4: each
// use is a ritual). The ritual, repeatable, leaves a charge in its city (`ritual_charge`); a unit in
// that city spends it on one of three weathers centred on a plot within 10 plots of the city, over
// the plots within 5 plots of that centre, for the rest of the turn and the next 5:
// - Blizzard: units there do not heal and start their turns with one move fewer (never below one);
// - Storm: SHOOT and BOMBARD actions deal half damage in battles there;
// - Fog: no SHOOT actions in the first round of battles there, and units there are hidden from
//   other teams that have no unit or city within 1 plot of them.
// Rules: crates/ffh-core/src/ffh/cards/world_spells_2.rs (the weathers: `Game::area_effects`).
{
  "techs": [
    {
      "type": "TECH_CARD_WEATHER_ENGINE",
      "description": "TXT_KEY_TECH_CARD_WEATHER_ENGINE",
      "help": "TXT_KEY_TECH_CARD_WEATHER_ENGINE_HELP",
      "civilopedia": "TXT_KEY_TECH_CARD_WEATHER_ENGINE_PEDIA",
      "advisor": "ADVISOR_MILITARY",
